Further to our discussion, DLA was instructed as follows - [~accountid:60e96a31131bf80069e1459f] Please let me know ASAP tomorrow morning if I misunderstood any of the conditions as set out below. Obrigado\!

+*Email to DLA, 23 May:*+

{color:#0747a6}Our Country Manager Nuno has agreed on commercial terms with the biggest taxi association in Madeira, called AITRAM.{color}

{color:#0747a6}Could you please prepare a draft of a partnership contract in PT, with an unchecked EN translation for my benefit - unless it's not a lot more expensive to have it in dual language? {color}

{color:#0747a6}The commercial terms that have been agreed for the partnership agreement are as follows:{color}

{color:#0747a6}+*First 2 months (pilot phase):*+{color}

* {color:#0747a6}AITRAM must provide a minimum number of 50 taxis willing to register on the Bolt App to start the pilot phase.{color}
* {color:#0747a6}Bolt will run a number of campaigns:{color}
** {color:#0747a6}local (in Madeira) drivers marketing campaigns to communicate about the partnership;{color}
** {color:#0747a6}local (in Madeira) passengers marketing campaigns to try to increase the demand (e.g. campaigns on Facebook, Instagram, Google, etc); and{color}
** {color:#0747a6}local (in Portugal) airport campaigns that will promote Madeira airport.{color}
* {color:#0747a6}Bolt will not charge any commission to the taxi drivers who register after being referred by AITRAM (Intermediation Fee of 0%, as opposed to 25% as set out in clause 9.2 of the {color}[{color:#0747a6}Taxis T&Cs{color}|https://assets.ctfassets.net/tk7rwcciwvbq/68NXFyEWInG4SaZoGQnyBA/a8a7f1a54c23cc328e8cd811ffcd43ed/Portugal-TC-Taxi-Operators-09-11-2021.pdf]{color:#0747a6}).{color}

{color:#0747a6}+*After the first 2 months:*+{color}

* {color:#0747a6}AITRAM must provide a minimum number of 50 taxis (with the potential to reach 500, which is the total number of taxi associates in AITRAM).{color}
* {color:#0747a6}Bolt will pay AITRAM a monthly compensation to incentivize them to convince the taxis to affix the Bolt sticker on their car: for every taxi registered on the Bolt App which accepts to get the Bolt sticker affixed, Bolt will pay AITRAM 50€ per month per car (only if the minimum of 50 taxis is reached for that given month). {color}
* {color:#0747a6}Bolt will run a number of campaigns:{color}
** {color:#0747a6}local (in Madeira) drivers marketing campaigns to communicate about the partnership; and{color}
** {color:#0747a6}local (in Madeira) passengers marketing campaigns to try to increase the demand (e.g. campaigns on Facebook, Instagram, Google, etc).{color}
* {color:#0747a6}Bolt will charge a reduced commission to the taxi drivers who register after being referred by AITRAM: Intermediation Fee of 20%, as opposed to 25% as set out in clause 9.2 of the {color}[{color:#0747a6}Taxis T&Cs{color}|https://assets.ctfassets.net/tk7rwcciwvbq/68NXFyEWInG4SaZoGQnyBA/a8a7f1a54c23cc328e8cd811ffcd43ed/Portugal-TC-Taxi-Operators-09-11-2021.pdf]{color:#0747a6}).{color}
* {color:#0747a6}Initial term of the contract should be 12 months.{color}

{color:#0747a6}For background, I understand that AITRAM is a taxi association whose purpose is to defend taxi drivers' benefits and it also works as a dispatcher. Taxis have to pay a registration fee to adhere to AITRAM. In return, they get access to some discounts, offers and other benefits negotiated by AITRAM with third parties / providers. it is not an union, so hopefully this should not infringe any competition laws in PT. {color}

{color:#0747a6}One final clarification: the usual {color}[{color:#0747a6}Taxis T&Cs{color}|https://assets.ctfassets.net/tk7rwcciwvbq/68NXFyEWInG4SaZoGQnyBA/a8a7f1a54c23cc328e8cd811ffcd43ed/Portugal-TC-Taxi-Operators-09-11-2021.pdf]{color:#0747a6} will apply to the taxis which register through AITRAM. {color}{color:#0747a6}_As a second assignment, let's please discuss the need to create some PT T&Cs based on our_ {color}[{color:#0747a6}_Global Branding Terms_{color}|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/driver-vehicle-branding-terms/]{color:#0747a6}_. We'll be looking at an unpublished version of such T&Cs, perhaps signed only by the taxis._{color}


{color:#0747a6}Let me know if you need anything further at this stage. {color}

{color:#0747a6}Would it be possible for you to provide a draft partnership agreement {color}{color:#0747a6}+*by Wednesday 25 May COB*+{color}{color:#0747a6}? Could you please let me know your fees for this assignment (ideally with the price difference - if any - between a PT agreement with an unchecked EN translation and a dual language PT-EN agreement)?{color}

