So we see that notification events were created with 75 ms delta between them. They were delivered and processed at the same time by different nodes.

One notification with id 2100350601 was processed successfully, second with ID 2100350576 processed with error and error message is {{Payment row was not updated from pending status!}}

Error log written [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment/main/cron/notificationWorker.ts#L738-L740], bug happened [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment/main/table/paymentRow.ts#L427-L439]:

* First transaction calls payment row update to state {{finished}} [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment/main/table/paymentRow.ts#L409] with condition {{payment_row.state = pending}}
* Second transaction calls the same update code and got locked by DB, until first transaction commit or abort
* First transaction update payment state to {{captured}} and put payment status update event {{authorized}} to DB table
* First transaction commit the changes
* Second transaction unlocked and read {{payment_row}} table to find last record with {{finished}} state [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment/main/table/paymentRow.ts#L427] and it got data from snapshot created when transaction started: {{prepare finished}} + {{capture pending}}
* Then second transaction do {{payment.state}} update to {{prepared}}

To fix it we must abort {{payment_row}} + {{payment}} update transaction, if {{payment_row}} wasn’t updated.
Same bug could present in {{payment-core}} too

