*Meeting Notes 06.06.22*

*_Support Solutions (Masha):_*

* For SS Team, more people might be involved;
* We can’t control over what agents are doing and what is the PA rate; it’s also limited from the product side
* After looking into the issues for SD Portal, we should aim into simplifying the submission process (giving less options, the process does not leave too much space for different approach);
* The product Team should also be involved, so that there are no technical ways to go around SD submission and Content
* Discussing with TLs used. tobe a long process, often painful; we don’t yet know where is it coming from. Potentially TLs are simply responsible for their market metrics and they do not care about anything else (or not much else); the big picture is then missing; 
* Supportability is dealing with the same issues, simply because this local approach will always be a priority for TLs, they feel responsible and are ready to go out of their way to fix/improve it;
* Another idea is. to go through top management (Heads of verticals, even); 
* Also, sometimes local OPS Teams are pushing for something but if they are inventing something completely new, there is currently no filter to that. *What is the relationship between centralising processes and localised OPS needs?*
* Usually, local guidelines mean local procedures - *what are the main risks for this?* _The global approach is one thing - we want to have it, so that agents can switch markets and don’t have to learn anything from scratch; usually, it’s also easier to check how people are performing if we know that the same process is presented in all sites; it’s more cost-efficient; the riskiest part is when the process is related to Data PRivacy because this can cost the business a lot of money and/or reputation; SS Team is consulting with Legal Team to always make sure that the process doesn’t put us in any danger as a company; We also should. be aware of fraud - local and de-centralised approach can leave more space for little mistakes and cost us even more;_ 
* Restructuring KB is one of the SW Team’s ideas; Since KB isn’t easy to follow, agents sometimes try to create their own guides, for agents by agents.
* Local Guidelines are also coming from a good place but it’s not cost-efficient and can end up more problematic for us;
* Often with local teams local guidelines were rejected, even without any presented narrative;
* What we can do, as SS TEam, is to see the narrative, discuss and potentially give it a test-phase and check how does it work? SS Team will probably have a lot of questions;

*_ESC SPs site (Irena):_*

* The ESC SPs accountabilities are still in development; they are constantly changing what they’re supposed to do. Initially, it was tracking escalations and aim to reduce it;
* Since some markets reduced this issue, they use ESC SP as QA people which can be impacted by the Global Quality Team
* Some ESC SP check their Process Adherence;
* Themba is responsible for ESC Toolkit project on FD and Masego is working on Quality; Both involve ESC SPs;
* Some markets don’t have this point of contact, whenever they are needing some guidance in terms of localised needs; For Example - Irena and Matilda, when Irena was still an ESC SP;
* FD Agents/ESC SPs prepared some local guidelines for the OS Agents to help them; OS Agents can still insist on tips and tricks on a daily job;
* ESC SPs may still need more guidelines so that they are aware of what everyone is doing and what is the context of their work; How to contact KM Team with processes?
* Irena has an idea to create the guideline in the form of the training for any situation they need to contact KM. Why, what, how, where?
* Again, accountabilities between KM and CS Delivery have to be very, very clear in the case of implementing this change.

Other points:

* Notifying Heads and Regionals; be transparent about our idea and they need to. be supporting this; perhaps they can propose other markets; We need to make sure they are aware of these ideas;
* It’s better to do it officially and not “in the shadows”
* It gives us a good and safer route to try this approach
* RLs and STLs responsible for the ESC SP are changing, especially since they are not exactly having anybody specifically there; Themba is doing this “just because” - it seems there is not a proper structure on the top; 
* Notify about the markets, not necessarily ask
* Choice of markets can be also considered because UK is actually collaborating with the SS Team. a lot; perhaps Azerbaijan, where we are definitely live BUT there is not close collab just yet.
* Idea for the metric: Pre- and post- surveys for ESC SPs; questions about communication with us;
* Questions for help, etc. is hard to measure and track; Because it is dependent on the reaction from the OS Agents, we can’t really set this as a success metric;
* Process Adherence would be perfect as a measurement BUT it’s not being currently monitored closely everywhere and the same tool has to be used.

